}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{9}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=3x+\\frac{1}{2}$ for $x\\in [-9,9).$ The Fourier series of the $18$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524985 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53537d13-56ed-578b-89f6-12be53184c9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524985 #edb/ref 1074 "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=9$ and $f(x)=3x+\\frac{1}{2}$ for $x\\in [-9,9).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{9}{\\int }_{-9}^{9}(3x+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x]}_{-9}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}((\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {9}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9)-(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-9)^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-9))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(126-117) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524991 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186524895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524991 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341815" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524991 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524991 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of the function \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & x\\in [0,3) \\\\ -4, & x\\in [-3,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{2}.$\n\n${a}_{2}=$ {{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524991 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6138bd37-a9a0-5af4-80eb-ad7aa981c99c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524991 #edb/ref 1074 "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{L}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3.$ Also, $f(x)=1$ for $x\\in [0,3)$ and $f(x)=-4$ for $x\\in [-3,0).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{0}(-4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2\\pi }{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}x)]}_{-3}^{0}+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2\\pi }{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}x)]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi ))+\\frac{1}{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525083 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186525086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525083 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2f23af18-6fc6-51a2-9ae3-01f862c5c75a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525083 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186222023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525086 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186525109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525086 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a9f9a3f-bf20-54e7-9f47-aa598fef0e88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525086 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186372791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525109 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186525121 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525109 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8a15da49-604b-5a13-b749-afcedfa2e089" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525109 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186372797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525121 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186525130 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525121 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a7e42cee-7619-57a2-a6a6-5a997e4e2632" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525121 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186524985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525130 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cf1e87c7-8f9a-5050-a189-bceb0d6f5b0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417